But note that the comment contains %3C etc which are fine; we need to escape the double quotes inside the href string. The href value includes single quotes inside the SVG, which are fine because they are not double quotes. The outer double quotes around the whole string need to escape any double quotes inside. The href contains \" inside the string (the data:image...). Actually the href value is: data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 100 100'%3E%3Ctext y='0.9em' font-size='80'%3E🚀%3C/text%3E%3C/svg%3E

We need to escape the single quotes? Not needed, only double quotes need escaping. The href string uses single quotes for attributes, which are fine. The only double quotes inside are the ones around the whole href attribute value in the HTML, which we need to escape. In the JSON string, we need to escape the double quotes that appear inside the string. For example, in the line:

<link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 100 100'%3E%3Ctext y='0.9em' font-size='80'%3E🚀%3C/text%3E%3C/svg%3E\">

We need to escape the double quotes before icon and href. So we have \"icon\" and \"href\". Also the outer double quotes at start and end of the whole string need to be escaped as \". So the entire string will have many escaped quotes.

