Now we need to escape double quotes inside the string. The only double quotes are around attribute values: lang="en", charset="UTF-8", viewport content, link rel="icon", link rel="stylesheet", id="app", id="gameCanvas", id="timer", src="./game.js". Also the comment contains no double quotes. The href value contains single quotes, which are fine.

So we need to escape each double quote with \". Also need to escape backslashes (there are none). Also need to escape newline characters as \n.

Thus the string will be:

"<!DOCTYPE html>\\n<html lang=\"en\">\\n<head>\\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\\n  <title>Vibrant Game</title>\\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\\n  <!-- Emoji favicon -->\\n  <link rel=\"icon\" href=\"data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg xmlns='http://www.w3.org/2000/svg' viewBox='0 0 100 100'%3E%3Ctext y='0.9em' font-size='80'%3E🚀%3C/text%3E%3C/svg%3E\">\\n  <link rel=\"stylesheet\" href=\"./style.css\">\\n</head>\\n<body>\\n  <div id=\"app\">\\n    <canvas id=\"gameCanvas\"></canvas>\\n    <div id=\"timer\">00:00</div>\\n  </div>\\n  <script src=\"./game.js\"></script>\\n</body>\\n</html>"

Check that we escaped each double quote. For example, after <!DOCTYPE html> there is a newline \n. Then <html lang="en"> has a double quote after en, we need to escape as \"en\". Similarly for other attributes.

